[wait_input]
[background arg="res://arts/splash art/backgrounds/laboratorio.png" fade="0.0"]
I am back at the lab. I am more used to making the rounds, gathering reports from my assistants, and checking up on all the specimens in the inventory.
Once again, I approach L3XA.
[background arg="res://arts/splash art/backgrounds/laboratorio_zoom.png" fade="0.0"]
It feels different this time. I stare at their serene face, and it somehow looks familiar.
Being here, right next to it, I feel in the air a familiar sensation that I can’t quite describe.
The specimen also seems to be reacting to my approach. The closer I get, the more I see its facial muscles twitching.
It relaxes when I walk away from it. The computer monitor shows some alteration in the metabolic processes.
It’s nothing alarming, but it’s enough to go on my hourly report to the bridge.
I continue my rounds, absent-mindedly, when something else unusual happens.
stranger: I can feel you’re close to me. [br][pause]\
Can you still hear me…?
This voice. I recognize it.
I look around, trying to find the person who spoke to me. Nobody is paying attention.
stranger: I didn’t expect we would meet here, of all places.
My eyes turn in the direction of L3XA’s tank. The creature is still static, its eyes are still closed.
alien: So, you recognize me. I can feel your attention turning to me. Only I can’t look at you….
- RESPOND
	jump RESPOND
- PRETEND TO IGNORE
	set {fdp} += 1.0
	jump NOT LISTEN
label RESPOND
\doctor: Hey, excuse me?
Everyone at the lab stares at me. They look confused.
alien: They can’t hear me, silly. I’m speaking to you, only. Maybe it’s best if they don’t know I’m awake…
I guess I should say something so no one thinks I'm crazy.
\doctor: Uhmmm, I– can somebody get me the results of the last blood test on specimen 000-96?
alien: That was clever. It should do for now.
\doctor: ...
alien: There is a way you can talk to me as I’m talking to you now.
alien: Listen, try to form the words that you want to say in your mind and send them to me. Can you do that?
So I can just communicate with L3XA via telepathy? I should try it. There’s so much going through my head right now.
jump main
label NOT LISTEN
After a confused pause, I decide to continue walking as if nothing changed. I don’t know what’s happening right now, and I want to know more before I commit to a reaction.
alien: Are you listening to me right now? I know you are, you are the only person that can hear me.
I continue silent, trying not to show any disturbance on my face to any onlookers.
alien: You were more open to conversation when we first met. But I guess I spooked you.
Is L3XA really referring to last night’s… dream? What was that all about?
alien: ...I guess that you don’t know that you can talk to me like I do. If you form your thoughts in the shape of words and send them to me, I will pick up on them.
I decide to venture a response.
label main
[background arg="res://arts/splash art/backgrounds/laboratorio.png" fade="0.0"]
\doctor: ...can you hear me…?
join alien (teste/New portrait) center
alien: Yes, I can hear you. It’s been so long since I heard someone talking to me like this.
\doctor: This is very new to me… can we talk? I have some questions.
alien: Go ahead. Ask me anything.
\doctor: Okay so… how do you do this? The telepathy, I mean.
alien: It’s how my species communicates.
alien: However, in this state, I can’t hold our connection for very long.
alien: I would like to talk to you all day, but for now we only have some time before I slip into unconsciousness again.
\doctor: I think we should start with a proper introduction.
\doctor: Hello, I’m Dr. Daphnis. I’m here to help you.
alien: Help me…?
\doctor: Yes, I’m the Chief Medical Officer, and I’m here to make sure you get better.
\doctor: What is your name?
alien: I think you papers call me… L3XA
\doctor: Okay, we can use that name, then.
\doctor: You must have gone through a lot of pain lately, but I’ll make sure you feel as comfortable as possible.
alien: ... can you really do that?
\doctor: Yes, and you can help me. Tell me, how are you feeling, right now?
alien: It… hurts…everywhere…
\doctor: I’m going to increase your dosage of painkillers, okay
\doctor: Tell me, does that feel better?
alien: ... A little, yes
\doctor: Good. Can you move at all? like your fingertips?
alien: ... no, I don’t think so. my mind can talk to you, but I can’t move.
\doctor: It’s okay, that will do, for now.
\doctor: It’s important that you keep talking to me as I look at your stats.\
tell me…
- WHERE DO YOU COME FROM?
- WHY DO THEY CALL YOU DANGEROUS?
	jump WHY DO THEY CALL YOU DANGEROUS?
\doctor: Where do you come from? I've never seen someone like you before.
alien: I come from ancient, distant stars from another galaxy.
alien: y kind travels alone, going from planet to planet. We seek knowledge, which we learn from those that cross our paths.
\doctor: Sounds like us humans. We also seek answers in different star systems, and have done so since we were no longer stuck around a single celestial body.
alien: Our travel is not about finding answers, it’s about having experiences.
alien: We believe that this is our way of becoming eternal, living on the memories of others. Is their collective consciousness, we are one.”
\doctor: “This is beautiful. i never heard of this before. Your people are a wonderful form of life
\doctor: Is it too difficult  to find one of your people
alien: I wish I could see one of them again… But I think that I must wait until the time is right. We can’t rush things.
alien: It’s becoming more difficult every day.
\doctor: I’m going to make sure you get better to meet them once again.
alien: Thank you, Doctor
L3XA’s story is fascinating. But I have a feeling they aren't telling me everything. I wonder what happened to them.
jump main 2
label WHY DO THEY CALL YOU DANGEROUS?
\doctor: Perhaps it’s not a good moment to say this… but the crew seems to be somewhat… afraid of you. Can you tell me why?
alien: They would have warned you. It’s only natural.
\doctor: What do you mean?
alien: They didn’t tell you?
\doctor: They only told me to keep you alive.
alien: Don’t they want you to find things out about me?
alien: Like how I can speak to you, for example?
\doctor: No. I’m only here to help you.
alien: ... I really wish you could help me.
L3XA’s vital signs are becoming unstable
\doctor: I need you to keep calm okay? Listen to my voice. You’re going to be fine. let me give you a dosage of this…
Things seem to calm down
alien: Thank you, Doctor.
alien: You’re really taking good care of me.
alien: Don’t leave me.
\doctor: I won’t. I’m still with you
I feel uneasy… L3XA is very unstable. I wonder what can happen if she loses control…
label main 2
alien: I am becoming tired now… I have to let you go…
\doctor: L3XA, wait, I still need you to-
alien: ...Will you be okay…?
L3XA’s presence in my head is becoming weaker…
leave --All--
[background arg="#000000ff" fade="0.0"]
alien: “...meet me again tonight…”
…
This is it. I’ll have to wait until I can talk to L3XA… when they are ready again
Their situation is very delicate… If I make a mistake now, they may suffer the consequences…
This is… too much! The first time I ever talked with someone using telepathy! To think that it was even possible!
I’ll have to keep this under wraps for now. Cmd. Flagg can’t know about any of this.
I know full well that what I'm doing is treason. But I need to learn more before I can talk to anyone about this.
commander: “Don’t take your eyes off it for a second.”
Is what he said…
I can’t trust anyone just now…
I need to think…
…
Another long shift has come to an end.
I head to my quarters, and I’m ready for some night’s sleep.
they did say we would meet again…
jump chapter 4/